{{Term/Store|Hyrule Bass|Hyrule Basses|Series, OoT, OoT3D, TP, TPHD, BotW, TotK, HWL, HWDE, AoC, AoI|plural}} are recurring animals and [[Item]]s in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref name="E 65"/><ref name="BotW Inventory"/><ref name="TotK Inventory"/><ref name="HWL Dining Room"/><ref name="HWDE Dining Room"/><ref name="AoC Material"/><ref name="AoI Materials"/>

==Characteristics==
==={{OoT|-}}===
{{Stub|OoT}}

==={{TP|-}}===
{{Stub|TPHD}}
Hyrule Bass can be caught at the [[Fishing Hole]] and [[Eldin Spring]]. When caught on the hook they may leap out of the water in an attempt to break free.

==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Compendium/Extract|Hyrule Bass}}
In {{BotW}}, Hyrule Bass are commonly found in rivers and lakes all over Hyrule.<ref name="BotW Inventory"/> Link can eat them raw to restore a [[Heart]] to his [[Life Gauge]], or he can [[Cooking|Cook]] them in [[Meal]]s to gain more hearts. When used in Cooking] they provide no effects to Link when eaten unless cooked with another [[Material]]. They become a [[Roasted Bass]] when exposed to [[Fire]] or a [[Scorching Climate]] and a [[Frozen Bass]] when chilled. If a Hyrule Bass avoids getting caught, it will eventually mature into a [[Staminoka Bass]].<ref name="BotW Hyrule Compendium"/>

